Fall back for emoji to the registered fonts first on Apple platforms too

On macOS and iOS, Skia's paragraph falls back for an emoji by asking the default font manager for "Apple Color
Emoji" by name (FontCollection::defaultEmojiFallback), before it asks any font manager for the character, so
0001's order never reaches emoji there: they draw in the system's Apple Color Emoji whatever an app registers.
This answers that name with the registered font that draws emoji (the first that has U+1F600, in the face
nearest the style), when there is one; with none registered, the system's as before.

diff --git a/skiko/src/commonMain/cpp/common/FontMgrWithFallbackWrapper.cc b/skiko/src/commonMain/cpp/common/FontMgrWithFallbackWrapper.cc
index 993d1d7e2..458b02c48 100644
--- a/skiko/src/commonMain/cpp/common/FontMgrWithFallbackWrapper.cc
+++ b/skiko/src/commonMain/cpp/common/FontMgrWithFallbackWrapper.cc
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 #include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstring>
 #include "FontMgrWithFallbackWrapper.hh"
 #include "FontMgrDefaultFactory.hh"
 
@@ -24,6 +25,14 @@ sk_sp<SkFontStyleSet> FontMgrWithFallbackWrapper::onCreateStyleSet(int ix) const
 }
 
 sk_sp<SkTypeface> FontMgrWithFallbackWrapper::onMatchFamilyStyle(const char familyName[], const SkFontStyle& style) const {
+    // On Apple platforms Skia's paragraph falls back for emoji by asking for this family by name, before it asks any
+    // font manager for the character: answer with the registered font that draws emoji, when there is one, so emoji
+    // fall back to the registered fonts first too.
+    if (familyName != nullptr && strcmp(familyName, "Apple Color Emoji") == 0) {
+        if (auto emoji = fallbackFontProvider->fallbackForChar(0x1F600, style)) {
+            return emoji;
+        }
+    }
     return wrappedFntMgr->matchFamilyStyle(familyName, style);
 }
 
